## Consumer Group Partition Assignment

```
Topic: orders (6 partitions)

Consumer Group A (order-service):
├── Consumer 1 → partitions [0, 1]
├── Consumer 2 → partitions [2, 3]
└── Consumer 3 → partitions [4, 5]
Offset stored per partition: group-A reads from its own committed offsets

Consumer Group B (analytics-service):
├── Consumer 1 → partitions [0, 1, 2]
└── Consumer 2 → partitions [3, 4, 5]
Offset stored per partition: group-B reads independently from group-A
```

## Spring Kafka Consumer Group Configuration

```java
@Configuration
public class KafkaConsumerConfig {

    @Bean
    public ConcurrentKafkaListenerContainerFactory<String, OrderEvent> factory(
            ConsumerFactory<String, OrderEvent> consumerFactory) {
        var factory = new ConcurrentKafkaListenerContainerFactory<String, OrderEvent>();
        factory.setConsumerFactory(consumerFactory);
        factory.setConcurrency(3);  // 3 consumer threads — one per 2 partitions (6 total)
        factory.getContainerProperties().setAckMode(ContainerProperties.AckMode.MANUAL_IMMEDIATE);
        return factory;
    }
}

// Consumer with manual offset commit for at-least-once processing
@Component
public class OrderEventConsumer {

    @KafkaListener(
        topics = "orders",
        groupId = "order-service",
        concurrency = "3"  // alternative to factory.setConcurrency
    )
    public void consume(OrderEvent event, Acknowledgment ack) {
        try {
            processOrder(event);
            ack.acknowledge();  // commit offset only after successful processing
        } catch (Exception e) {
            // Don't acknowledge — message will be redelivered
            log.error("Failed to process order: {}", event.getOrderId(), e);
        }
    }
}
```

## Offset Management

```yaml
# application.yml
spring:
  kafka:
    consumer:
      group-id: order-service
      auto-offset-reset: earliest  # or: latest
      # earliest: start from beginning of topic (good for new consumers on existing topics)
      # latest: start from new messages only (good for consumers that don't care about history)
      enable-auto-commit: false  # ALWAYS false when using Spring @KafkaListener
      # Manual commits with Acknowledgment give you control over at-least-once delivery
```

## DefaultErrorHandler + Dead Letter Topic

```java
@Configuration
public class KafkaErrorConfig {

    @Bean
    public DefaultErrorHandler errorHandler(
            KafkaOperations<String, Object> kafkaTemplate) {

        // Retry up to 3 times with exponential backoff
        var backOff = new ExponentialBackOff(1_000L, 1.5);
        backOff.setMaxAttempts(3);  // 1s, 1.5s, 2.25s delays

        // After 3 retries, send to dead letter topic
        var recoverer = new DeadLetterPublishingRecoverer(
            kafkaTemplate,
            // Route to: {originalTopic}.DLT on partition 0
            (record, ex) -> new TopicPartition(record.topic() + ".DLT", 0)
        );

        var errorHandler = new DefaultErrorHandler(recoverer, backOff);

        // Don't retry deserialization errors — message is corrupt, retrying won't help
        errorHandler.addNotRetryableExceptions(
            JsonParseException.class,
            DeserializationException.class
        );

        return errorHandler;
    }
}

// Consumer
@KafkaListener(topics = "orders", groupId = "order-service")
public void consume(OrderEvent event) {
    // If this throws, DefaultErrorHandler retries, then sends to orders.DLT
    orderService.process(event);
}

// Dead letter consumer — for inspection and replay
@KafkaListener(topics = "orders.DLT", groupId = "order-service-dlt")
public void consumeDlt(
        @Payload OrderEvent event,
        @Header(KafkaHeaders.RECEIVED_TOPIC) String topic,
        @Header(KafkaHeaders.OFFSET) long offset,
        @Header("kafka_dlt-exception-message") String exceptionMessage) {
    log.error("Dead letter message: topic={}, offset={}, error={}, payload={}",
        topic, offset, exceptionMessage, event);
    // Alert ops team, store for manual review, etc.
    alertingService.notifyDltMessage(topic, offset, exceptionMessage);
}
```

## @RetryableTopic — Annotation-Based Retry

```java
// Alternative: retry topics instead of blocking main topic
@Component
public class OrderConsumer {

    @RetryableTopic(
        attempts = "4",   // 1 main + 3 retry topics
        backoff = @Backoff(delay = 1000, multiplier = 2),
        // Creates: orders, orders-retry-0, orders-retry-1, orders-retry-2, orders-DLT
        exclude = {DeserializationException.class}  // no retry for these
    )
    @KafkaListener(topics = "orders", groupId = "order-service")
    public void consume(OrderEvent event) {
        orderService.process(event);
    }

    @DltHandler
    public void handleDlt(OrderEvent event) {
        log.error("Exhausted retries for order: {}", event.getOrderId());
    }
}
```

## Ordering with Partition Keys

```java
// Ensure all events for one order go to the same partition → ordered
@Service
public class OrderEventProducer {

    private final KafkaTemplate<String, OrderEvent> kafkaTemplate;

    public void publishOrderEvent(OrderEvent event) {
        kafkaTemplate.send(
            "orders",
            event.getOrderId().toString(),  // KEY → same key = same partition = ordered
            event
        );
    }
}
```

